In Adobe's Flash (now Adobe Animate) with ActionScript 3.0, you can use the `TextField` class to display text in columns. To force a `TextField` to display text in columns, you can set the `textAlign` property to `TextField.LEFT` and use the `wordWrap` property to `true`. Additionally, you can set the `multiline` property to `true` to allow the text to wrap to the next line.

Here's an example of how you might set up a `TextField` to display text in columns:

```actionscript
import flash.text.TextField;
import flash.text.TextFormat;

// Create a new TextField instance
var myTextField:TextField = new TextField();

// Set the text format for the TextField
var myFormat:TextFormat = new TextFormat();
myFormat.font = "Arial";
myFormat.size = 12;
myTextField.defaultTextFormat = myFormat;

// Set the text alignment to left
myTextField.textAlign = TextField.LEFT;

// Enable word wrapping
myTextField.wordWrap = true;

// Enable multiline
myTextField.multiline = true;

// Add the TextField to the stage
addChild(myTextField);

// Set the text to display in columns
myTextField.text = "This is an example of text that will be displayed in columns. " +
                   "The text will wrap to the next line when it reaches the end of the TextField's width.";

// Set the width of the TextField to a fixed value to force column display
myTextField.width = 200; // Set this to the desired width
```

This code will create a `TextField` that displays the text in columns, wrapping the text to the next line when it reaches the end of the `TextField`'s width. Adjust the `width` property to control the number of columns displayed.

